{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Please do not refrain, etc.</b> That is, according to what the first emissaries said — for his own inclination was what held him back from going with them — therefore they said to him that he should be willing for this measure of honor and not refrain, etc. And this is because he lacked awareness of the suspicion they suspected of him, namely that these were his own words and not HaShem's. He [Balak] thought that the intention was to tell him not to be concerned about HaShem's words and to go without His approval; therefore he [Balaam] answered, <b>If Balak gives me, etc.</b> I am unable — meaning, even though I would wish to do it, for the disposition of a wicked man was upon him and he was a rebellious servant against his Master, nevertheless he is not master of free choice and will in this matter."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:12:36.724362314Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}